Once I learned of the spell enhancement effect of robes I even
started using robes with combat wombats.  Attack spells rule.  It's
also a matter of taste that I do not object to killing
always-peacefulls
including priests.  Show me a cross-aligned priest and I'll do some
prep and with a high chance show you a robe, often even two robes.
Knowing about prayer-protection I don't value purchased protection
as much, either.

My ascension kit armor tends to look like: "oR, teeshirt, GDSM,
robe, speed boots, dexterity gloves, brilliance helm.

For classes that can't #twoweapon, a reflection shield acheives
redundant reflection and any sign of trouble switching to an "oLS.
For classes that get MR from their Quest artifact that acheives
redundant MR.  Both types of redundancy are good but not
required for my playstyles.

Reasonable variations range to: "oLS, teeshirt, SDSM, [oMR,
jumping boots, power gloves, any helm leaving similar possibilities
for redundant reflection and MR but not the spell enhancement of
a robe.

If I get the amulet in Sokoban, I'm going to want GDSM.  If I get
the bag in Sokoban, I remain undecided between GDSM and SDSM.



